00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:14.360
Bitcoin allocation to your TFSA last month through BTCX when cross-asset signals turned positive.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:20.600
Your order filled cleanly because the ETF trades on the TSX with tight spreads during market hours.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:26.900
Yet the position still moved 12% while the rest of your equity sleeve rose only 4%.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:34.360
The mechanism at work is Bitcoin's historically low correlation to equities around 0.2 to 0.4 in

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:40.280
normal regimes that improves the efficient frontier by lifting expected return for a given level

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:49.340
of risk when kept between 1 and 5%. Canadian investors gain an extra edge by holding BTCX or ETX

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:55.640
inside a TFSA, avoiding both capital gains tax drag and the custody headaches of self-managed

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:02.220
wallets. Professionals always check the 30-day rolling correlation before sizing up. If it spikes

00:08:02.220 --> 00:08:09.300
above 0.6, they reduce or exit because the diversification benefit has collapsed. The biggest mistake

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:14.980
with crypto allocation is treating it like a growth stock and letting it exceed 5% of the portfolio.

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:22.000
Instead, set a hard 3% target, rebalance annually, and treat anything above that threshold as

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:28.940
